<title>UK: London sugar freight ends week quietly.</title>
<headline>London sugar freight ends week quietly.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The suagr freight sector ended the week on a quieter note with just a few fixtures and new orders reported.</p>
<p>FIXTURES - CSR have now finally fixed 16,000 bulk for Apl 1/10 Queensland to Japan and 26,000 for end March/Early April Queensland to China, no rates.</p>
<p>Dreyfus have fully fixed 26,000 bulk Cuba to Black Sea or Baltic end March.</p>
<p>NEW ORDER - Andre 26,000 bulk sugar Cuba to Iran end March/Early April.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
</text>
